Main Purpose of the Job
To provide and deliver exceptional marketing support and service to the Branch Agents and Branch Management through collaboration and alignment with the Regional Marketing structure. The scope of work may include coordinating ad-hoc project outputs ranging from content creation, design, video editing, social media management and reporting.
This is a branch-based position in the Pretoria Region and reporting to the Pretoria Regional Marketing Manager.
Key Responsibilities
Manage all submission of briefs received from Agents in the branch for their marketing campaigns;
Liaise with the Agent and Regional Marketing on the execution of briefs and communicating any updates or changes on the brief from the agents and marketing;
Liaise with internal and external stakeholders on timing and deliverables of various projects, ensuring briefs are actioned and content delivered on time;
Ensure delivery of collateral to the various stakeholders on time and in full;
Manage traffic daily on project management;
Update information on our website, specifically for Branch Developments, ensuring accuracy, as and when applicable;
Management of our marketing server and Marq, ensuring that folders are organised appropriately;
Managing submissions to Regional Marketing for all branch and national publications and media;
Briefing of external email campaigns;
Liaise with Agents to create content for social media campaigns, and briefing to Regional Marketing for execution as and when required;
Liaise with Agents to create hyper-local campaigns and ensure delivery thereof;
Create digital and print marketing collateral from Marq templates and Alchemy as required. Keep up to date with templates available and communicate to agents;
Liaise with external suppliers when necessary;
Manage accounts with marketing suppliers and ensure timeous payments;
Manage branch signage contracts and renewals, liaise with signage suppliers alongside Branch Managers;
Train agents on how to use new marketing collateral as and when developed by Regional and or National Marketing;
Assist Regional Marketing with any branch marketing events, expos, agent activations or meetings.
Brief geotargeted hyperlocal social media campaigns in collaboration with Regional Social Media Coordinator and ensure delivery thereof;
Manage, coordinate and give feedback on all leads that are generated from each campaign;
Monitor and communicate the progress of each campaign to the agent and Branch Managers;
Manage the collation of property collections and ensure adequate distribution across all channels;
Ad-hoc support to Agents with the design and printing of brochures and drops, or creating Digital versions;
Any other duties as and when may be required by management that are within the area of your expertise.
Key Competencies
Process driven – pulling together briefs, chase lists and plans from various sources per campaign and ensure delivery against these on time and in full;
The ability to build relationships with internal stakeholders with a willingness to actively support the Agents, Branch Managers and the Regional Marketing team;
Deadline driven with the ability to multi-task, whilst maintaining the quality standards of delivery;
Self-motivated and energetic;
Attention to detail and enhanced accuracy;
Must work well under pressure and easily adapt to change;
Self-motivated and energetic.
Education & Experience
A relevant qualification in Digital and/or Traditional Marketing;
2+ years of experience in a Co-ordinator role within a Marketing department;
CMS or CRM platform (Email, website, ) experience is essential;
Experience in programmes such as Marq, WordPress, MS Powerpoint, MS Word, Excel, Outlook, Google Products is essential;
Experience in Adobe and In Design will be an added advantage;
Social Media and Design experience will be an advantage;
Previous experience working in an Agency environment will be advantageous.
Knowledge & Skills Required
Project management skills – working with competing deadlines, managing input and sign-off from stakeholders, ensuring that collateral is ready for campaign go-lives;
Excellent traffic management skills and the ability to work with designers and additional stakeholders;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
Excellent organisational and administrative skills;
Proven abilities in Social Media Management (Community Management and scheduling);

